@startuml

' =============================================================
' UC-005 Operations Board - Phone List Coordination
' Use Case Overview (CIM)
'
' MDA Level: Computation Independent Model
' Perspective: Business / Conceptualization
'
' This diagram captures the business need at Slottet residential
' care facility, using only domain language. No system, no IT,
' no technology references. Terms like "operations board" and
' "phone list" are domain terms used by the staff at Slottet.
' =============================================================

title UC-005 Operations Board — Phone List Coordination (CIM)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam usecaseBackgroundColor #FFF9E6
skinparam actorBackgroundColor #E8F4FD
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

' --- Business actors (real roles at the residential care facility) ---
actor "Caregiver\non Shift" as Caregiver
actor "Shift Coordinator" as Coordinator

' --- Business domain boundary ---
package "Slottet — Shift Phone Coordination" <<Business Domain>> #F8F8F8 {

    usecase "See which caregiver carries\nwhich work phone for this shift" as UC1
    usecase "Take responsibility for a\nwork phone during my shift" as UC2
    usecase "Release my work phone\nat end of shift" as UC3
    usecase "Identify which caregiver to\ncontact for a resident concern" as UC4

}

' --- Business relationships ---
Caregiver --> UC1
Caregiver --> UC2
Caregiver --> UC3
Coordinator --> UC1
Coordinator --> UC4

note bottom of "Slottet — Shift Phone Coordination"
    <b>Business context:</b>
    Slottet is a 24-hour residential care facility for residents
    with special needs. Caregivers work in Day, Evening, or Night
    shifts. During each shift, fixed work phones are carried by
    specific caregivers so that colleagues and residents can
    reach the right person.

    <b>Today (paper-based):</b>
    Phone-to-caregiver assignments are tracked on a paper handover
    form. Hard to keep current; easy to lose; no history.

    <b>Domain rules:</b>
    - Phone numbers are fixed: 41522, 41523, 41524, 41525, 41526, 41527, 41529
    - Each phone is carried by one caregiver per shift
    - Shifts: Day, Evening, Night
    - The phone list is for identification — not a contact list

    <b>What this CIM does NOT contain:</b>
    No system, no screens, no input fields, no save buttons.
    Those are platform-independent and platform-specific concerns
    handled in PIM and PSM.
end note

@enduml
